  "materialNarrowings": {
    "S2": "Independent verification remains valuable, but A08/A09/D02 show evidence value and evaluator interpretation can diverge; a correct evaluator is not assumed at discovery time. Verification systems themselves remain revisable.",
    "S3": "HD3 strengthens the applicability-scope narrowing. Pearl Street local DC, locally rational automobile routes and Ford specialization are genuine improvements in bounded worlds even when they do not survive radically different world conditions. Generalization is required only across the materially different conditions implied by the declared claim/scope; it is not a prerequisite for every local improvement to be real.",
    "S5": "Structured standards, potency units, safety rules, experimental archives and statistical representations provide non-Agent persistent-state examples, but many physical inventions still have no direct S5 analogue.",
    "S7": "Ford/Wardenclyffe/Wegener force separation of current scoped value, future option value and future production-function improvement. Major value need not be metaproductive, and metaproductive potential can coexist with declared-objective failure.",
    "S9": "Authority/admissibility must bind the concrete consequence domain. Expertise in bacteriological cause did not transfer to tuberculin therapy; technical communication capability did not itself establish maritime operating obligations; employer ownership did not authorize unsafe egress."
  },
